  "id": "0c2ccbe1-2837-538f-bdb8-4b7d24357f7a",
  "slug": "family-sicilian-sauce-and-meatballs",
  "name": "Family Sicilian Meatballs and Sauce",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Sicilian meatballs are simmered in a rich and hearty meaty sauce that's made from scratch and served over pasta for a crowd-pleasing Italian meal.",
  "cuisine": "U.S. American Italian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "To make the meatballs: Combine bread and milk in a medium bowl. Mix in ground beef, eggs, Romano cheese, parsley, salt, and pepper; form into meatballs and place into the freezer to firm up."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "To make the sauce: Heat 3 tablespoons olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add onion; cook and stir until onion has softened and turned translucent, about 5 minutes. Add garlic and 1 sausage link; cook about 3 minutes more."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile, in a large skillet over medium heat, brown beef chunks and pork neck bones; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "When onions and garlic are done, turn heat down to low. Add tomato paste and cook for a few minutes. Stir in the browned beef and pork, crushed tomatoes, wine, bay leaves, cinnamon, parsley, basil, and salt and pepper. Bring sauce to a simmer, then reduce the heat to low and cook for 3 to 4 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Heat remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large skillet; Brown meatballs and remaining sausage links in batches. Add to sauce and simmer for 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "When sauce is nearly ready, bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Add pasta and cook for 8 to 10 minutes or until al dente; drain."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Remove pork neck bones from the sauce; discard. Serve meatballs and sauce over hot pasta."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 24,
